From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Davison <gdavison@hashicorp.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:34:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Merge pull request #50519 from
 arditti/f-wafv2-web-acl-rule-scope-down-logical-prune

resource/aws_wafv2_web_acl_rule: support logical statements in `scope_down_statement` and only allow nestings AWS WAF accepts

diff --git a/.changelog/50519.txt b/.changelog/50519.txt
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..9c7c8372237b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changelog/50519.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+```release-note:bug
+resource/aws_wafv2_web_acl_rule: Fix `scope_down_statement` not supporting logical statements (`and_statement`, `not_statement`, `or_statement`), including `not_statement` nested inside `and_statement`
+```
+
+```release-note:bug
+resource/aws_wafv2_web_acl_rule: Reject `managed_rule_group_statement`, `rate_based_statement` and `rule_group_reference_statement` nested in `and_statement`, `not_statement` or `or_statement`, `and_statement` directly in `and_statement`, `or_statement` directly in `or_statement`, and `and_statement` or `or_statement` with fewer than 2 statements at validation time, in both `statement` and `scope_down_statement`, matching AWS WAF
+```
